  - 'Welcome. This is the hillside behind the old farmhouse. Take a slow walk with
    the dogs.


    You can get the dogs ready in Dress in your personal menu. In
    VR, hold the right stick down. On Desktop, press T. On mobile, tap Menu on the
    screen.


    If there is anything you want to know, choose it on the left.'
  - 'Welcome. First time here? Take these for getting ready for a walk: {0} points.
    Just this once.


    You can get the dogs ready in Dress in your personal menu.
    In VR, hold the right stick down. On Desktop, press T. On mobile, tap Menu on
    the screen.


    If there is anything you want to know, choose it on the left.'
  - Menu
  - Petting
  - The dogs
  - Photos
  - Shopping
  - Treats
  - Goodbye
  - Call
  - 'First, try opening your personal menu. In VR, hold the right stick down. On
    Desktop, press T. On mobile, tap Menu on the screen.


    There are 7 tabs at
    the top. Dress lets you put accessories on a dog. Treats brings a treat to your
    hand. Call lets you call a dog over and choose a pose. Toys brings a dog''s ball
    back to you. Live lets you host a show in the garden. Particles lets you choose
    the petting glow. Play has the dog-eye camera and Trainer play.


    Press Points
    at the top to learn how to get points or enter a gift code. Settings has Volume,
    Night mode, language and photo resolution. There are radio and distance fade
    settings too, both for PC only. If you are the administrator, you will also find
    options to let everyone call dogs and host live shows. The administrator is the
    owner of this instance. If the owner is absent, the Master takes over. You can
    also reread Getting started from Information in Settings.


    Press Close when
    finished. In VR and on mobile, use the same input you used to open the menu to
    bring it back to you, even if you left it far away. On Desktop, T switches between
    opening and closing it.'
  - 'Pet the top of a dog''s head, cheeks, or under its chin. Dogs enjoy being petted
    with one hand, but they love it with both hands, and the light effects change
    too.


    Choose petting effects in the Particles tab of your personal menu.
    Some are free, some cost points, and some come with live show purchases.'
  - 'Left to themselves, the dogs chase and play with each other. When they start
    playing like that on their own, anyone can watch for free. When tired, they drink
    water and lie down to rest. Just watching is fine, too.


    Each dog has its
    own ball color and size. Throw its ball and it will bring it back. On Desktop,
    hold the mouse button to charge, then release to throw. In VR, pretending to
    throw while still holding the ball may get a bark or a glance.


    Lost a ball?
    Open Toys in your menu and press Bring here for that dog. You cannot recall it
    while someone holds it or the dog is playing with it.


    I explain how to
    call a dog over to sleep beside you in Calling dogs.


    On the Dogs in the
    garden board beside me, you can name each dog and choose a favorite. Press the
    ? on the board to learn more.'
  - 'As you play with the dogs, memorable moments become photos on the photo board
    by the veranda. Photos of sleeping beside a dog appear in the bedroom. Each kind
    of photo has its own slots, and once those are full, the oldest ones are replaced.


    These
    photos are yours alone. Other people see different photos. They disappear when
    you leave this world. If you find one you like, on PC or Quest, point your VRChat
    camera at it and take a picture to keep it. On mobile, tap the photo to enlarge
    it, then take a screenshot. You can choose a frame for free.


    The dog-eye
    camera is a tool you buy with points. You can use it from Play, and only you
    can see its view. It is separate from these photos.


    For more details, press
    the ? on the photo board. To stop photos being taken or change their quality,
    open Resolution settings beside it.'
  - 'You receive 100pt on your first visit. The first time you talk to me, I give
    you another 100pt, just once. After that, you earn 1pt each minute just by relaxing
    here. Petting dogs and throwing balls do not earn extra points. You can receive
    points through gift codes too. Your points are shown on this board and in your
    personal menu. To use a code, press Points in your personal menu.


    There
    are 4 kinds of things here.


    Things you can enjoy for free. Petting dogs,
    throwing balls, calling dogs, and joining shows and play hosted by others.


    Things
    you buy with points. For toys and treats, press an item on the shelf and buy
    it from the confirmation screen. Other point purchases are in your personal menu.
    Treats are used up as you give them, but the others only need to be bought once.


    Things
    you buy once from the VRChat store. These include toy and accessory sets, and
    live shows. Some are only on sale for a limited time.


    The monthly membership
    is VAnimal Trainer. You buy a membership period to use it, and it does not renew
    automatically. From Play, you can host group gatherings and races, or choose
    2 available dogs to play with each other. Other people can join in for free without
    being members. See Information in Settings for more details.


    To host a
    live show, you must be the administrator and own that show. The administrator
    is the instance owner, or the Master if the owner is absent. With Live hosting
    for all: ON, others can also host shows they own. This starts out ON. Only one
    show can run at a time, and after it ends there is a short wait before another
    can begin. Check the screen for the waiting time. Anyone can watch for free.
    Some shows feature the dogs too.'
  - 'Choose Treats in your personal menu, then press Give. The menu closes when the
    treat is ready, so go ahead and offer it to a dog.


    Hold it and dogs come
    closer. Let go and the nearest dog eats it. You can have one treat out at a time.
    I have given you 5 treats to start with. When you run out, exchange points for
    more in Treats.'
  - 'Open Call in your personal menu, choose a dog and a pose, then decide where
    it should go and which way it should face. The dog walks over and rests there.
    To let it roam freely again, select it in Call and press Let roam.


    Dogs
    on a leash cannot be called. Release them first.


    Side sleep, Lie down,
    Sit, and Curl up are free. Other poses and actions can be added with points.


    Dogs
    can be called by the room owner (or the Master if the owner is absent), and by
    everyone when Calling open to all is ON.'
